<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for April 4.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for April 4.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Thursday released the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period April 2 to 4.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = millon cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 02 (actual) 211 mcm, 49 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 03 (forecast) 230 mcm, 54 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 04 (forecast) 236 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Apr 02 (actual) 10.9 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 03 (forecast) 7.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.2 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 04 (forecast) 8.5 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.3 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
